<h2>Searching the ISFDB</h2>
The ISFDB supports simple searches of the database. Name, Title, and
Series searches must consist of a single substring of the target for
a match to occur. Search comparisons are caseless, and the space character
is consider part of the search string. For instance, if one were to 
execute a name search on the string "d b", the result would be:
<pre>
   Search For Author: d b

   Found 13 matches 
   -----------------------------------------------
   <b>David B. Kisor</b>
   <b>Lloyd Biggle, Jr.</b>
   <b>Jand Beauclerk</b>
   <b>Stephen King</b>  (as Richard Bachman) 
   <b>Donald Barthelme</b>
   <b>Edward Bryant</b>
   <b>Richard Bowker</b>
   <b>Reginald Bretnor</b>
   <b>David Brin</b>
   <b>Richard Bowes</b>
   <b>David Bischoff</b>
   <b>Alfred Bester</b>
   <b>Donald Benson</b>
</pre>
The four search methods currently supported by the ISFDB are:
<ol>
  <li><i><a name="2A">Searching by Name</a></i>.
  Searches match on both authors and pseudonyms. Search results are a list of
  author hot-links to their Summary Bibliography. In the case of pseudonyms, 
  the citation consists of the author's actual name followed by 
  (as <i>pseudonym</i>); the pseudonym is not a hot-link, as the bibliographic
  data will appear on the actual author's bibliography. If the search string
  matches both the author and a pseudonym, only the actual author citation
  will be displayed. 
  <p>
  If only one author match is found, the author's summary bibliography is
  immediately displayed, instead of the match results.
  <p>
  <li><i><a name="2B">Searching by Title</a></i>.
  Searches for titles result in a list of title/author citations, where the author
  anchor is a hot-link to a Summary Bibliography. Titles are listed in alphabetical
  order, separated by category. For instances, a title search for "venus", results in:
<pre>
   Search For Title: venus

   Found 14 matches 
   -----------------------------------------------

   <i>Novels</i>
   Carson of Venus             <b>Edgar Rice Burroughs</b>
   Escape on Venus             <b>Edgar Rice Burroughs</b>
   Lost on Venus               <b>Edgar Rice Burroughs</b>
   Pirates of Venus            <b>Edgar Rice Burroughs</b>
   The Venus Belt              <b>L. Neil Smith</b>
   Venus Plus X                <b>Theodore Sturgeon</b>
   Venus of Dreams             <b>Pamela Sargent</b>
   Venus of Shadows            <b>Pamela Sargent</b>
   Venusian Adventure          <b>E. C. Tubb</b>

   <i>Collections</i>
   Venus Equilateral           <b>George O. Smith</b>

   <i>Shortfiction</i>
   Come to Venus Melancholy    <b>Thomas M. Disch</b>
   Dawn Venus                  <b>G. David Nordley</b>
   The Vanishing Venusians     <b>Leigh Brackett</b>
   Venus and the Seven Sexes   <b>William Tenn</b>
</pre>
  <p>
  <li><i><a name="2C">Searching by Year</a></i>.
  Since the database has entries across multiple centuries, year 
  targets must be complete, four digit strings (i.e.: "1984", not "84").
  The match list will display all works first published in the target
  year. The list will be displayed in the same manner as the title search
  above.
  <p>
  <li><i><a name="2D">Searching by Series</a></i>.
   A series search utilizes the same search rules as a Name or Title
   search, but matches on series names. If a match is found, all of the
   titles in the series are listed, as well as their hot-linked authors.
   For instance, doing a series search on the string "jedi", results in:
<pre>
   Search For Series: jedi

   Found 3 matches 
   ----------------------------------------------------
   <i>The Jedi Academy Trilogy</i>
   Champions of the Force         <b>Kevin J. Anderson</b> 
   Dark Apprentice                <b>Kevin J. Anderson</b> 
   Jedi Search                    <b>Kevin J. Anderson</b> 
</pre>
</ol>

